{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/327929-how-to-create-an-angel","id":327929,"title":"How to create an Angel ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-01T23:38:24-08:00","id":327929,"title":"How to create an Angel ?","content":"Currently for my game I'm trying to make a angel but I can't really find any rules in the book for it. I saw a few examples and they brought up some questions.<br /> So for example do angels have two forms like demons ?<br /> Because the book shows angel by the name of Mr Shiver but not once does it talk about what his true form looks like only his current one.<br /> <br /> When creating an angel is there any rule I need to follow ?<br /> <br /> Currently I'm making an angel that is going to exist with in a Command and Control Infrastructure. This angel is hooked into every camera and drone in the city made by the company and it is tasked to monitor and send angels out to locations of demon activity.<br /> <br /> So far I was thinking description wise it looks like a slim frail human being and it sits crossed legged unmoving as it is hooked up to millions of different wires. It has 4 arms that type on many different keyboards and has eyes all over its head to watch all the Screens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 12-02-2014, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T00:17:48-08:00","id":327953,"title":"","content":"Like someone said in your other thread that started about the subject, the rules for ephemeral entities are in the Appendix II; the mechanical guidelines in Demon: the Descent start on p.338. The rules are for ephemeral beings as a whole - the rules absolutely work for angels, but the given Numina and other stuff are written to be very general so they can be used across types. That section will point you in the right direction, but don't be afraid to write something more specific if you need it for your game - I personally have some tweaks lined up for angels in my game.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, angels do not by default have two forms; angels that do so probably have the Mortal Mask Numina or a similar effect. I know some folks have argued that an angel can be designed to look exactly like a normal human and forgo the need for something like Mortal Mask, which accounts for all the human or mostly human looking angels in Demon/GMC without the Mortal Mask numina; it's up to you if you want to run with that or not.<br /> <br /> The concept you've listed is entirely appropriate for an angel, though it sounds like most of it's &quot;effects&quot; are plot devices rather than actual mechanics - which is fine! There's absolutely nothing in the rules that would stop you from creating that angel, and it's not a bad option at all. If I was in your position I might consider making that thing a Cryptid instead, but that's just an aesthetic difference. In any case, good luck putting it together!<br /> <br /> That should start you off, if you have any other questions let us know. I'm probably going to be putting together an opinion piece to follow this up right after I post this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T01:09:49-08:00","id":327977,"title":"","content":"Okay, soapbox time: I feel like it's important to point out some of the descrepancies between how the fluff treats angels and how the mechanics portray them; whether you accept the differences or work to reconcile them, I think it's worth talking about in order to skip a big source of confusion early on.<br /> <br /> In the Demon text, angels are treated mostly like Demons with a couple of extra limitations. They talk a little about how angels are tied to Infrastructure and that they have access to Twilight, but the majority of the text portrays loyalists as beings that are fundamentally indistinguishable from the Unchained, to the point that you should have no idea if the person you're talking to is human, angel or demon. Infiltration is presented as a high priority concern, and if hunter angels are sent after you they will chase you to the ends of the earth with no issue. Example angels are usually human or semi-human looking, and limitations for how long they can stay in the field are never discussed.<br /> <br /> The mechanics point a much different animal: an angel's ephemeral nature and their ties to Infrastructure have a lot bigger impact than the fluff would suggest. Infrastructure is extremely important to angels, as it's both fuel source and staging ground for Manifestations. Also, let's look at the practicality of infiltrating the Unchained by going over fundamental differences between angels and demons.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Demons are inherently physical creatures that can go wherever they want. Angels are ephemeral beings that have to use the Materialize, Possession or Claimed to walk the world physically, each which have their own issues. Looking just at Materialize as a baseline, an angel has to start in Infrastructure to use it (technically the Infrastructure has to be Open but a Rank 1 angel can achieve that with a single Essence), the Manifestation lasts for 1 hour per success and then it dumps you back into Twilight. Deep cover is nearly impossible under these conditions. Even in the short term, Mortal Mask is not infallible even considering the angel's likely high Finesse; by my reading, users of Mortal Mask wouldn't enjoy the penalty if a demon uses Aetheric Resonance, which isn't automatic but is a major issue if the angel is trying to pull one over on a paranoid demon.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Despite loyalists having the more ephemeral bodies, the Unchained's identities are much more mutable. Short version: demons can switch covers and change into their demonic form. An angel trying to blend it almost certainly lacks these abilities.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Unchained can sense Aether, while angels can't. Any test for Demon-hood factoring that in will be almost impossible for an angel to pass.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Hell, angels don't even have the ability to lie perfectly. The problems of infiltration without that are pretty self-evident.<br /> <br /> I could keep going but as long as you're looking for it the issues jump out, so I'm not going to waste your time. The way I handle the discrepancies in my game? Well, honestly most of the time I accept that the differences are there and shift the focus to compensate. Angels in my demon games are going to be the familiar but ultimately alien Other, a host of ephemeral agents that serve the G-M from the shadows and stay within bastions of power for the most part. For horror and paranoia related to infiltration and betrayal, I won't hesitate to use regular humans or possibly some cryptids, but by and large my workhorse is going to be other Unchained.<br /> <br /> And for those times where I need an angel that works like the angels in the fluff? Well, I have some tricks up my sleeves...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T04:45:57-08:00","id":328051,"title":"","content":"Kirby--<br /> <br /> Yes, absolutely. I was flabbergasted by the discrepencies, too. You can get by them with homebrewed, Angel-specific Manifestation Effects and Numina, if you want (i.e. maybe Angels don't use Covers, but they have a special Claim Manifestation that allows them to Claim several beings at once and jump between them. It would be different from Demons, since when you &quot;leave&quot; one Claimed body, they probably continue living normally, accepting everything you did in their bodies as their actions, rationalizing them, etc., which would be interesting in and of itself). But yeah, the discrepencies are annoying; it makes it hard to try to understand what the writers were going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T08:14:21-08:00","id":328223,"title":"","content":"Point of order:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/327929-how-to-create-an-angel?p=327977#post327977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Hell, angels don't even have the ability to lie perfectly. The problems of infiltration without that are pretty self-evident.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire purpose of a significant number of Messenger angels would likewise indicate that treating a lack of direct statement to the effect of their having this ability as proof that they don't is an assumption that doesn't scan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T10:07:47-08:00","id":328354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/327929-how-to-create-an-angel?p=328223#post328223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order:The entire purpose of a significant number of Messenger angels would likewise indicate that treating a lack of direct statement to the effect of their having this ability as proof that they don't is an assumption that doesn't scan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I should have put a note about this in that sentence, but in any case the text kinda points to a trend of angels using mind-altering Numina and Influence to complete their missions; they aren't so much perfect liars as they are excellent at warping minds and making people believe. Most of the time it's a semantic difference, but in the case of trying to pass as an Unchained to another Unchained the differences seem like they could be a big liability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:03:32-08:00","id":328443,"title":"","content":"I've run two short Demon games now and I just outright ignore the ephemeral rules. Each angel is a custom built A.I. loyal to the GM. Whether a cultists got that intelligence downloaded into their mind, a human body was built from scratch, a robot was made to house the angel or any other form it could possibly be. It is still an angel. some are impossible to tell apart form human or Demon, some can body jump, some live wholly on the internet as a living virus.<br /> The only trick is defining what you want it to be(form), what it can do(numina/stats) and what are it's limits(bane/ban). I also make a big deal out of how it was summoned.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an example:<br /> Viso Born into this world time and time again through the reflected light of a far away star where it lies dormant between summons. the cultists differ each time but there procedure is the same. they catch angelic light in holy mirrors gifted to them by God. The trapped light loops impossibly in the reflection until a host body steps into the light (the perfect spot for angel-jacking). Viso enters the host it's blistering radiance whipping away all thoughts until only the divine words remain. Its mission is to identify and observe the unchained. in the host body Viso looks completely human unless it is using it's powers which manifest as bleeding light. <br /> Rank 2<br /> Power:3 finesse:5 resistance:3<br /> Numina: Teleportation, invisibility, mind wipe, <br /> Bane: Viso looses apart of it's self when it's host body comes in contact with a reflective surface.<br /> Ban:it scope is limited to areas touched by the light of its star. at most a couple miles diameter from it's summoning circle, adjust for plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T12:52:01-08:00","id":328559,"title":"","content":"As a note to fooling aether resonance: confiscated stockpile<br /> Which raises the question of what the machine does with a demons possessions... g.m. Cultists might have gadgets from captured demons<br /> <br /> On topic: demon form makes sense to give to angles under comparable limitations, as do select embeds and tailored covers immune to compromise while attached (gm fixes holes) because even if demons use things in different ways they still had to gain the hardware somehow. Pacts I'd say keep as demon only for flavour and to spark questions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T21:34:42-08:00","id":328879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/327929-how-to-create-an-angel?p=328354#post328354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose I should have put a note about this in that sentence, but in any case the text kinda points to a trend of angels using mind-altering Numina and Influence to complete their missions; they aren't so much perfect liars as they are excellent at warping minds and making people believe. Most of the time it's a semantic difference, but in the case of trying to pass as an Unchained to another Unchained the differences seem like they could be a big liability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this ignores the whole &quot;exiles are trusted by neither angels nor demons&quot; thing and how becoming an exile robbing you of the ability to lie perfectly doesn't seem like a reasonable outcome in light of that.<br /> <br /> There's also the whole running theory about the Machine being like the Unchained writ large, which loses plausibility if its agents don't benefit from the same epistemic filter while working for it as while not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T01:01:47-08:00","id":328985,"title":"","content":"Technically speaking an angel is perfectly capable of mimicking an Unchained's ability to switch covers via the Mortal Mask numen. It says, specifically, that it -can- be used during Manifestation, not that it must be used. It also doesn't specify that the ability makes the entity appear like a specific human chosen at entity-creation and the ability to perceive past this would be the equivalent imperfection for an angel that a Demon suffers via compromise. It's just when an angel screws up, God doesn't care (though the demons do!). The problem, however, lies within the essence conundrum where eventually hopping in this manner between individuals is costly on the essence pool.<br /> <br /> A more long-winded technique is to write-up generic NPCs (such as office workers, police, etc) that serve the role of possess-fodder and have hunter angels able to hop back and forth via possession much like an Agent from the Matrix trilogy. It is achievable via having each hunter have the Seek numen and to assume that there are many small pieces of infrastructure across the city. This is more mechanically trying, but since the mechanics happen in the background, it will create the image that the angel is able to just pop out from every door. Mechanically, of course, he is possessing a host, shooting some guns, leaving and popping into a new one and so forth. In light of the above option (and the fact that any Demonic Form ability or Exploit/Embed can be made into numen) it would seem better to have an angel with Mortal Mask and Urban Fluidity, but it works thematically well.<br /> <br /> It is therefore simple to give an angel a &quot;demonic form&quot; by giving it a horrifying base design and several images via Mortal Mask. When it wishes to assume its true form it simply turns off the mortal mask numen and gets creative.<br /> <br /> My personal rule for defeating the essence conundrum is to treat it like NPC willpower pools by having short-hand limitations. (This character has half of his essence in this scene, next scene he has it all back again, because he's assumed to be restoring it and using it off-screen).<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: For clarity.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 12-03-2014, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T05:28:09-08:00","id":329134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/327929-how-to-create-an-angel?p=328985#post328985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically speaking &lt;SNIP&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I love all of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T12:15:33-08:00","id":331378,"title":"","content":"I personally get past the whole Manifestation issue by allowing the G-M to activate Manifestations for it's Angels.<br /> <br /> And the God-Machine gets an arbitrary number of successes. Because it's the <i>G-M</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:44:16-08:00","id":331530,"title":"","content":"If I need a sudden angel appearance I just assume that the needed infrastructure is there (cultists sacrificing and what not), if the ring decides to try and stop the angel by messing with the infrastructure then I flesh it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T10:41:09-08:00","id":334336,"title":"","content":"Is there any indication of what I should do with &quot;demonic form&quot; for angels? I mean, a demon with a granade launcher should probably have been an angel with a granade launcher...all demonic form parts are all cool and everything, but a rank 1 angel has a hard time simulating all that fucking armory of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T07:48:28-08:00","id":335183,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would probably just use Numina and fluff it at that point. You know, Blast covers projectile weapons, Drain is done by a syringe in the forearm, note that your unarmed attacks to lethal if the angel has swords for hands, etc. If the Numina provided in Demon don't cover it, you can always write your own with the form in mind, and if you don't think they have enough Numina at the beginning you could always give them a number of Form Numina that can only be used when the angel's nature is fully revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T18:54:10-08:00","id":335666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/327929-how-to-create-an-angel?p=335183#post335183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I would probably just use Numina and fluff it at that point. You know, Blast covers projectile weapons, Drain is done by a syringe in the forearm, note that your unarmed attacks to lethal if the angel has swords for hands, etc. If the Numina provided in Demon don't cover it, you can always write your own with the form in mind, and if you don't think they have enough Numina at the beginning you could always give them a number of Form Numina that can only be used when the angel's nature is fully revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, Splintered City: Seattle has Tower's variant of Blast as a go-to example to this sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T19:30:40-08:00","id":335697,"title":"","content":"If the angel is a one-and-done antagonist, I'd probably avoid issues like a fully-fledged Angelic Form. I've always liked the idea that angels- being, you know, angels -aren't as limited as other Ephemeral beings, so I've always had it that angels get to ignore some of the rules. If an angel's already shown up, I think it's safe to assume that the Infrastructure and Open conditions are satisfied. I've had it that if anything that can be Urged, Controlled, Possessed, or Claimed walks into Infrastructure or within the jurisdiction of that particular Infrastructure instantly receives the Open condition, and then the angel can do what it wants without contest provided it succeeds its roll. Otherwise, the angel can simply force a particular Manifestation with a contested roll- except for Possession and Fetter, which remain uncontested.<br /> <br /> If the angel is a reoccurring antagonist, I'd suggest going all out. Stats, a full-on Angelic Form, everything. I've always given my angels access to any Embeds they could need in fulfilling their mission, and use Numina in the place of Exploits since it would be unthinkable to an angel to try and force too much power through an Embed and risk overloading an occult matrix. If an angel starts throwing around Exploits, then you know you've got an angel on the edge of Falling. In terms of angels possessing Cover, I've always assumed that because the Unchained can angel-jack, that angels with missions of sufficient length are given Covers instead of just possessing a random person/animal/thing or assuming a Mortal Mask. It states that any high-rank angel with the ability to use high-powered Influence (at least the ability to permanently create one thing, so at minimum a Rank 4 angel) can create Infrastructure for itself or another angel. So lets assume in this case that the Infrastructure would be a Cover, and the Linchpin would be killing the person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}